 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yoma.45a.1",
   "daf": "45a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "שֶׁדּוֹמֶה לְפָז. זָהָב שָׁחוּט — שֶׁנִּטְוֶה כְּחוּט. זָהָב סָגוּר — בְּשָׁעָה שֶׁנִּפְתָּח כָּל הַחֲנוּיוֹת נִסְגָּרוֹת. זְהַב פַּרְוַיִם — שֶׁדּוֹמֶה לְדַם הַפָּרִים.",
   "en": "«because it resembles the luster of pearls [paz]» in the way it glistens. «Shaḥut gold» is named as such «because» it is very malleable and «is spun like thread [shenitve keḥut].» Shaḥut is a contraction of the words shenitve keḥut. «Closed gold» is so called «because when» a shop «opens» to sell it, «all the» other «shops close,» as no one is interested in purchasing any other type of gold. «Parvayim gold» is so called «because» its redness «resembles the blood of bulls [parim].»"
  },
  {
   "id": "yoma.45a.2",
   "daf": "45a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "רַב אָשֵׁי אָמַר: חֲמִשָּׁה הֵן, וְכׇל חַד וְחַד אִית בֵּיהּ זָהָב וְזָהָב טוֹב. תַּנְיָא נָמֵי הָכִי: בְּכׇל יוֹם הָיָה זְהָבָהּ יָרוֹק, וְהַיּוֹם אָדוֹם — וְהַיְינוּ זְהַב פַּרְוַיִם שֶׁדּוֹמֶה לְדַם הַפָּרִים.",
   "en": "«Rav Ashi said: There are» in fact only «five» types of gold, the last five in Rav Ḥisda’s list. Gold and good gold are not independent categories; rather, «each and every one» of the types of gold has two varieties: Regular «gold and» a superior variety called «good gold. That was also taught» in a baraita with regard to parvayim gold: «On every» other «day» the coal pan was made «of greenish gold, but» on «this day» it was made of «a red» gold, «and this is the parvayim gold which resembles the blood of bulls.»"
  }
 ],
